WEBVTT

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:06.200
Let's see... flathead.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:10.000
Flat... head...

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.330
Oh, there it is!

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:16.120
"Bartail flatheads usually
live in the sandy bottoms

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.290
as low as 30 meters below the surface.

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:20.830
They are considered a delicacy."

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.200
Ah, I see.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:27.910
"Their bodies are horizontally flat.
Their heads resemble the back of a shovel.

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:30.160
They blend in with the sand,

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.500
hiding their appearance,
and feed on smaller fish that happen by."

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.370
"Picture of a bartail flathead"

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.000
"Picture of a bartail flathead"

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.750
"Picture of a bartail flathead"
So this is a flathead...

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:42.370
So this is a flathead...

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.620
What a weird face.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:51.620
Thank goodness!

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:55.370
I don't know what I'd do if it
really was that creepy-looking thing.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:56.370
"Hisssss"
I don't know what I'd do if it
really was that creepy-looking thing.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:57.080
"Hisssss"

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:00.290
Curse you, Natsumi.

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:05.120
I mean... It doesn't look
too big, so I think I'll be okay.

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:09.040
But seriously... its face is so weird.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:11.950
Hina, ya done in here?

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:15.250
Yup, I'm good. Thanks, Dad.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.120
What were ya lookin' up?

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.700
The fish we're catching tomorrow.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:23.290
I'll enjoy 'em with some drinks.
Make sure ya catch plenty again.

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:24.450
Leave it to me!

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.000
Good girl.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.660
Aren't I?

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:05.160
All righty, we all here?

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.450
We're gonna be fishing at Kamegahama today.

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.040
Kamegahama?

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.250
Kamegahama Swimming Area.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.950
It's right around the curve over there.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:16.040
Was that always there?

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:19.410
Flatheads live in the sand.

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:22.870
The breakwater round here is nothin'
but rocks, so you won't find any here.

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:25.000
I looked them up last night.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:28.330
They blend into the sand
and eat smaller fish, right?

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:31.080
Well, aren't you studious?

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:34.700
Natsumi! The thing you
showed me wasn't a flathead at all!

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:37.660
I told you... that was a frilled shark.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:42.000
B-By the way, Prez, are we actually
lugging all this to Kamegahama?

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.660
It's not far, but walking with all
this stuff would get a bit tough.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.200
Huh? Really?

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:53.330
Ya think I'd actually go through all
the trouble of luggin' all that around?

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:56.120
Ohno, bring the thing around.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:57.410
The thing?

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:01.790
"Sea King"

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:03.580
"Sea King"

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:07.450
"Sea King"
The all-purpose trolley, Sea King!

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:08.540
"Sea King"
A pull cart?!

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:08.830
A pull cart?!

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:11.160
No, I just said it was Sea King.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.790
It's totally a pull cart.

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:14.250
Wait, we're using this?

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:15.540
Heck yeah.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:17.750
B-But it's so embarrassing.

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:22.700
Then y'all can carry
them coolers filled with ice.

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:27.330
But seriously, why a pull cart?

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:30.620
The old fishermen gave it to us.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:31.660
Hina,

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:35.580
why don't we keep our
distance from them as we walk?

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:37.580
Oh, come on. No need to hold back.

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:39.580
Y'all can totally hop on if ya get tired.

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:40.660
Huh?!

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:40.950
--I-It's okay, really!
--Thanks for your concern, but...

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:44.160
--Go on, Ohno. Get 'em in.
--I-It's okay, really!
--Thanks for your concern, but...

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:45.370
Huh?

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.040
Well? Ya comfy?

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:53.160
Oh, whatever already...

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:57.620
Y'all look like a family that
just finished up some farm work.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:58.830
Hey!

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:01.540
Hup...

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:03.660
I'll put the net in here, too.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:05.660
Okay.

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:07.330
Tsurugi.

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:11.160
Make sure ya take care of yer own rod.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:12.830
Okay.

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.410
My own fishing rod...

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:21.790
You can stick your rod in here.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:28.000
How convenient. It's like that's
exactly what it's made for.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:32.500
Our <i>senpai </i>made some modifications
so it'd be more convenient for us to use.

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:34.040
Wow...

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:36.790
Right, looks like we're ready to go.

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:39.040
All right, let's go.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:41.200
Yeah!

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:06.500
Are we there yet?

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:09.620
Jeez, you never have any energy, Hina.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:13.870
Hey, Natsumi!

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:15.450
Jeez...

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:17.290
Hina, look!

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:21.000
We can actually see it!

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:27.870
We're here.

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:29.040
Let's go, Hina!

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:30.290
Okay!

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:31.830
Make sure ya don't fall.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:33.500
Okay!

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.660
It's so pretty!

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:50.000
And we've got it all to ourselves.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:53.500
I guess it is a weekday and off season.

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:56.330
Don't you remember coming here together as kids?

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:59.250
Wait, we did?

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:00.870
Hey!

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:03.750
Come over here!

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:05.620
We're gonna fish over here.

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:07.450
Okay!

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:13.950
Right, so first, I'm gonna explain
how we're gonna catch these things.

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:15.370
Thanks!

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.700
I like yer enthusiasm.

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:20.790
Ta-dah! Soft lures.

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:22.870
They're artificial bait made outta rubber.

00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:24.580
They also call 'em "worms."

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:28.330
Basically, they think they're
real fish and try to eat 'em.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:30.000
You're right. They're soft.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.500
You put 'em onto a special kind of hook.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:35.580
Ta-dah! A jig head.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:37.660
They're weighted hooks.

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:42.160
Ya take this sucker and go like this,
then this, and then this...

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:43.700
And there ya go.

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:51.160
And then ya cast this sucker. Whoosh... splash.

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:53.660
Oh, yeah. Imagine my arm as the sandy bottoms.

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:56.200
She's starting something...

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:58.450
Swim, swim, swim...

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:05.330
Once the lure lands, lift up
yer rod and bring the lure up...

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:09.830
Then ya drop it... Lift it up again,
and drop it again, over and over...

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:13.410
Then sometimes, just drag
that sucker along the sand.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:16.200
Rinse and repeat and...

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:19.700
Chomp!

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:21.660
Then ya just need to reel that sucker in.

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:23.080
Easy, right?

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:24.370
Sure...

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:27.330
Here ya go. Go ahead and make yer own rig.

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:28.910
Okay.

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:35.120
Um... How exactly do you tie the line to this?

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:37.700
Ooh, me! Me! Leave this to me!

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:40.910
All right, let's do this together.

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:42.450
Okay.

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:46.410
First, pull the line through
the hoop on top of the jig head.

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:48.790
Then wrap it back around the
line about five times like this.

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:49.700
Uh-huh.

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:53.540
Then you pull the line back
through the first hoop you made,

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:55.700
then pull it through here and...

00:08:57.790 --> 00:08:59.870
If you make it a little wet with your spit,

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:02.790
it'll lessen the friction
and the line will stay strong.

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:04.330
I see...

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:07.040
And then, grab the end of the line...

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:09.910
Then pull the end of the line
still attached to the rod, and...

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:14.200
There you go.

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:17.250
Now all you need to do
is cut off the excess line.

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:18.250
Okay.

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:21.750
I did it.

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:24.450
It's sort of similar to a thread knot.

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:26.830
It's called a clinch knot.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:28.910
Remembering how to tie them will come in handy.

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:30.620
Wow...

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:33.160
So how do you attach the soft lures?

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:34.700
Leave it to me!

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:37.290
Th-Thanks for your help...

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:38.450
So the longer tail of the lure is the bottom.

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:39.580
"Top"
"Bottom"
So the longer tail of the lure is the bottom.

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:40.620
"Top"
"Bottom"
Uh-huh.

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:42.330
You chop off its head,

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:48.330
then line it up with the jig head and
try to see where the hook will come out.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:49.580
When you insert the hook,

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:51.830
the top and bottom are
gonna be reversed, so be careful.

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:54.750
Oh, right. Because the hook is curved.

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:58.290
When you stab it, try to aim for the center.

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:02.370
It's gonna be a little hard,
but do your best to push it through...

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:06.160
And when the end of the hook
is about where you eyed it before...

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:07.870
...push it through.

00:10:09.410 --> 00:10:12.450
Then you push the head all the way down, and...

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:15.200
Once the lure's all straight again, you're set.

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:18.450
If the lure's all bent,
the flathead's gonna be suspicious.

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:21.160
Wait, mine's really bent.

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:26.120
When that happens, pull it back out a bit
and adjust where the hook comes out.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:27.660
O-Okay...

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:33.790
We did it!

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:35.410
Yay!

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:37.200
Okay, I'm gonna do this.

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:41.120
I promised Dad I was gonna catch him a bunch.

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:44.830
The flatheads are pretty big,
so you really only need to catch one.

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:46.330
Huh?

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:50.950
When they're really big, you can
catch one that's about 60 centimeters.

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:53.410
Big...?

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:58.290
What?! No one told me that!

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:01.410
You should've realized that
when the bait are little fish...

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:04.450
I can't touch anything that big!

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:06.790
I'm scared! I'm so scared!

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:08.450
Hina.

00:11:08.450 --> 00:11:10.830
Have you ever heard this saying?

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:14.790
Don't count your chickens before they hatch.

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:17.830
You can worry about all that
after you actually catch one.

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:19.080
Wha...?

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:23.830
Well, considering how weak yer back is,
ya probably won't catch one that quickly.

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:25.700
Don't worry too much.

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:28.000
What?!

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:33.040
"Diary of Our Days at the Breakwater"
"Report 03 'Flatheads'"

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:39.410
The blue sky... The white clouds...

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:42.120
The clear, blue ocean.

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:43.910
And...

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:46.540
...so much garbage.

00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:51.160
President Kuroiwa, all I've been
catching is seaweed and garbage.

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:53.370
Yeah, I haven't gotten a bite either.

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:56.410
I mean, I guess I don't
mind if I don't catch one.

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:59.200
Even if I do catch one,
I hope it's as small as possible...

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:00.830
Sixty centimeters!

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.830
Looks like Hina and Prez
aren't having much luck either.

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:10.870
Flatheads are pretty hard to catch at times.

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:14.910
Well, Hina has some beginner's luck.

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:18.290
Yes. I hope she catches one.

00:12:19.790 --> 00:12:24.120
All right! I'm gonna catch
a bigger one than Hina!

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:29.700
Ohno-<i>senpai</i>, this spot sucks!

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:32.000
Let's find another spot!

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:35.200
Wait!

00:12:36.410 --> 00:12:39.660
Natsumi and Ohno-<i>senpai</i>
are switching spots again.

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:45.000
It's called run and gun.
Ya just keep changin' fishing spots.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:48.580
There're times ya have better luck
actually catching something that way.

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:49.910
Ah...

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:53.330
You're not gonna go, President?

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:56.290
I'm just gonna chill right here.

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:03.290
Do you not care if you catch
anything or not, President?

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:04.620
Hm?

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:08.120
You don't ever seem that aggressive...

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:12.500
Well, I'd obviously prefer to catch something.

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:17.950
But my goal isn't to actually catch the fish...

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:21.250
Ah...

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:29.580
Again? Are there actually flatheads here?

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:32.290
I mean, I'm fine if I don't catch any...

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:35.290
But it'll bum me out
if I don't catch any either.

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:39.950
Maybe the flathead sees right through you.

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:41.120
It's seeing through me?

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:42.000
"Lifeless"

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:44.410
"Lifeless"
If the way yer movin'
yer lure about is pretty lifeless,

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:47.290
"Lifeless"
the fish will figure out they're not real.

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:47.950
the fish will figure out they're not real.

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:48.370
"Irregular"
the fish will figure out they're not real.

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:51.450
"Irregular"
If you wave yer rod around
in big strides, then smaller ones,

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:54.290
"Irregular"
and then stop... You basically have
to keep doing irregular movements

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:57.040
"Irregular"
to make it look like it's actually alive.

00:13:57.040 --> 00:13:57.620
to make it look like it's actually alive.

00:13:57.620 --> 00:14:00.580
Are fish that smart?

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:03.450
Way smarter than ya think, Tsurugi.

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:05.450
Huh...

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:08.830
It's good to close your eyes
and try to think about how

00:14:08.830 --> 00:14:12.120
the lure's actually movin' about in the water.

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:14.580
Oh... I'll give it a try.

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:16.870
There!

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:25.450
Close my eyes... and imagine...

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:30.700
Hey, it's lighter.

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:32.870
It must've hit the bottom.

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:40.450
I can feel it scraping along the sand.

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:43.410
Wow...

00:14:43.410 --> 00:14:46.250
I guess you can sorta tell even
if you can't see into the water.

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:50.410
It's important to get to know what
the ocean feels like with yer fingertips.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:52.000
Right.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:54.000
Come on, flatty...

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:56.910
I'm a delicious little fish...

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:59.870
Look how lively I am.

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:03.950
I'm absolutely delicious.

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:05.540
Move irregularly...

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:09.000
...like it's actually alive.

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:20.290
Ya surprisingly don't like losin', do ya?

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:22.080
Curse you, flathead!

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:24.160
Hup!

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:25.290
Take that!

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:28.870
There!

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:31.790
Take that! And that! And that!

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:38.910
Hup!

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:47.910
Seriously, again?

00:15:50.450 --> 00:15:53.500
I'm being pulled in!

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:55.330
Hey, wai--

00:15:55.330 --> 00:15:56.790
President...

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:59.120
Calm yerself, Tsurugi.

00:15:59.120 --> 00:16:01.450
Come on, straighten yer rod.

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:06.500
Plant the end of the rod into
yer stomach and hold on tight.

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:07.830
I'm scared...

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:10.910
Wait! Don't let go yet!

00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:12.660
--Wait! What am I supposed to do?

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:14.080
--Look, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>!
--Wait! What am I supposed to do?

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:14.500
--Look, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>!
--I'm being pulled in!

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:15.950
--Yeah.
--I'm being pulled in!

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:18.910
Don't panic. Just reel 'em in, nice and slow.

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:21.750
It's so heavy that I can't even...

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:26.080
This might actually be a flathead.

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:26.750
--Huh?!

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:27.200
--And a big one.
--Huh?!

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:28.910
--And a big one.

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:36.540
It's a flathead!

00:16:42.700 --> 00:16:46.700
Put your back into it, slouchy!
You got a big one!

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:48.540
Shut up!

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:01.330
Be careful.

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:04.750
Th-Thank you so much...

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:07.250
Nice catch, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>!

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:12.080
There, there. Now they're
all tired out and calmed down.

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:15.750
Tsurugi, keep luring them right over here.

00:17:15.750 --> 00:17:18.830
O-Okay...

00:17:18.830 --> 00:17:21.330
There ya go... Keep 'em steady...

00:17:23.450 --> 00:17:25.120
Congrats.

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:28.450
This is an excellent flathead.

00:17:28.450 --> 00:17:31.080
Awesome! Way to go, Hina!

00:17:31.080 --> 00:17:32.330
Congratulations.

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:40.660
I was so scared!

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:44.700
I thought I was going to
get dragged into the ocean!

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:50.790
Ugh! What's your problem, you stupid fish?!

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:56.370
You look weird! You're all flat! Ugh!

00:18:01.540 --> 00:18:04.660
Why are you laughing?!

00:18:09.450 --> 00:18:12.500
Guess you're the only one
that caught one, Tsurugi.

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:16.450
Boo. I wanted to catch one, too.

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:18.620
I think I'm done with flatheads...

00:18:18.620 --> 00:18:23.040
It's hard to catch big ones
like that. You should be happier.

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:26.450
Okay.

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:28.080
Everything's ready.

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:30.580
Okay. In that case...

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:32.500
Tsurugi, start filleting the fish.

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:34.540
Huh?! Me?

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:38.000
Of course. You're the one who caught it.

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:41.620
I can't, I can't, I can't,
I can't! There's no way!

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:44.330
Yeah, I figured as much.

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:48.450
Guess we don't have a choice.
Ohno, do it for her.

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:51.620
Thank you very much...

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:55.750
But in return...

00:18:57.700 --> 00:19:02.330
You need to finish 'em off.
That's your responsibility for catching it.

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:06.620
Finish it off?

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:08.410
I mean kill it.

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:09.950
Kill?!

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:16.040
Got it?

00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:17.830
Y-Yes...

00:19:19.250 --> 00:19:22.040
Wh-Wh-Wh-What am I supposed to do?

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:23.700
Right here.

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:28.950
Stab it right here, until you reach
the cutting board underneath.

00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:32.950
The spine's pretty hard,
so be careful not to slip.

00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:35.250
O-Okay...

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:56.080
Just get it done, already.

00:19:56.080 --> 00:19:58.790
If ya don't hurry up,
yer just prolonging its suffering.

00:19:58.790 --> 00:20:02.450
Come on, I'm starving! Hurry up!

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:13.080
--It looks so good!

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:14.830
--The blood... The blood...
--It looks so good!

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:16.750
--Its insides...
--It looks so good!

00:20:16.750 --> 00:20:19.870
Right, then. The one who
caught it gets the first bite.

00:20:19.870 --> 00:20:23.620
Huh?! O-Oh, okay... Wait, whoa!
When did all this happen?

00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:25.660
You just realized this?

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:28.750
The sashimi's chilling with some ice.

00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:30.700
I deep fried the rest.

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:33.250
Way to go, fishmonger's daughter.

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:36.450
Guess you're fit to be a bride any day.

00:20:36.450 --> 00:20:39.660
O-Okay... Let's dig in.

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:55.870
Nothing beats eating
the fish you caught yourself.

00:20:55.870 --> 00:20:59.910
Yeah, I definitely feel that...

00:20:59.910 --> 00:21:03.500
It's even better if ya fillet
and cook it yerself.

00:21:03.500 --> 00:21:06.450
Ya need to learn how to do it yerself next time.

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:09.080
I-I'll do my best.

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:17.830
Taking responsibility for catching it...

00:21:22.790 --> 00:21:26.830
Here you go. This one has a special
bonus for the person who caught it.

00:21:26.830 --> 00:21:29.040
Ooh, I wonder what it is.

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:32.040
Thank you very mu--

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:43.540
Guess she needs to get
used to fish a wee bit more.

00:21:45.410 --> 00:21:49.290
But that sure is a talented way to faint.

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:54.040
The head is so yummy, too. What a waste.

00:21:56.080 --> 00:21:58.290
Today's haiku...

00:21:58.290 --> 00:21:59.790
"The ocean garbage,

00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:01.330
the more garbage you pick up

00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:02.870
the cleaner it gets."

00:22:02.870 --> 00:22:04.120
By Natsumi.
